# Windsurf Rules — thin wrapper. Do not add unique rules here.

All governance for this repository lives in the canonical, vendor-neutral document at the repo
root: AI_CONSTITUTION.md. Read and obey it before generating or editing code.

Load-bearing rules (the constitution is authoritative):
- Reuse first: search registries/*.json and existing components/patterns/templates before
  building. Anything genuinely new is created in the Design System first, documented, recorded
  as an ADR (if significant), given a changeset, and only then used in the IGA product.
- Two products, one arrow: the IGA product consumes the Design System; the Design System never
  imports the product.
- Never hardcode colors/spacing/radii/elevation/motion — consume tokens/theme. Extend MUI
  rather than rebuilding it.
- Every screen ships loading/empty/error/success states, is accessible (WCAG 2.1 AA),
  permission-aware, and uses the repository/service data layer, not localStorage/fetch directly.
- Think before coding, ask when unclear, keep changes surgical.

If this file conflicts with AI_CONSTITUTION.md, the constitution wins.
